From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: DEBUG fault-inject a decode stall

DEBUG ONLY -- deliberately NOT in patches/kernel/series. It exists to test
the watchdog recovery path in patch 0057 on demand, because waiting for a
malformed stream to stall the engine by luck is not a test one can run twice.

sunxi_cedrus.fault_stall_hevc=N programs the next N HEVC slices with a bit
length four times the data actually queued. The VLD then starves waiting for
bits that were never sent and the engine stalls the way it does on a real
truncated stream -- which matters, because the alternative fault injections
(skipping the trigger, or finishing the job early) test a watchdog firing on
an engine that is perfectly healthy, and prove nothing about recovering one
that is not.

Bounded on purpose. Four times a slice length is a few hundred kilobytes at
most, the VE is behind the IOMMU on this board (patch 0042), and the count
decrements, so one write buys exactly one stall and the very next decode is
expected to succeed. That "next decode" is the measurement.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h265.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h265.c
@@ -414,6 +414,24 @@
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * DEBUG ONLY -- fault injection for the decode-timeout recovery path
+ * (sunxi_cedrus.fault_stall_hevc). Set it to N and the next N HEVC slices are
+ * programmed with a bit length four times the data actually queued, so the VLD
+ * starves waiting for bits that are not there and the engine stalls exactly as
+ * it does on a genuinely malformed stream. The watchdog then fires on a real
+ * hardware stall rather than on a job that was never triggered -- which is the
+ * difference between testing the recovery path and testing nothing.
+ *
+ * It is deliberate that this cannot be reached without being asked for: the
+ * count is zero unless somebody writes to it, and it decrements, so one write
+ * buys one timeout and the engine is expected to work again immediately after.
+ */
+static int fault_stall_hevc;
+module_param(fault_stall_hevc, int, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(fault_stall_hevc,
+		 "DEBUG: stall the VE on the next N HEVC slices (bit length x4)");
+
 static int cedrus_h265_setup(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx, struct cedrus_run *run)
 {
 	struct cedrus_dev *dev = ctx->dev;
@@ -492,6 +510,13 @@
 	cedrus_write(dev, VE_DEC_H265_BITS_OFFSET, 0);
 
 	reg = slice_bytes * 8;
+	if (fault_stall_hevc > 0) {
+		fault_stall_hevc--;
+		reg *= 4;
+		v4l2_info(&dev->v4l2_dev,
+			  "FAULT INJECTION: programming %u bits for %zu bytes of slice data\n",
+			  reg, slice_bytes);
+	}
 	cedrus_write(dev, VE_DEC_H265_BITS_LEN, reg);
 
 	/* Source beginning and end addresses. */
